ixel art layout confirmed, now focusing on the visual display.\n\nPlanning a Python script to render the pixel art as a high-resolution image using an image library, calculating the required dimensions. Column widths are calculated, and a 68px width is determined for each of the 8 columns. The overall image dimensions will be explored further, including considering 720px width and 920px height for the full picture with card elements.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python -c \"\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFont\n\nimg = Image.new('RGB', (800, 780), '#082313')\nd = ImageDraw.Draw(img)\n# Draw rounded table\nd.rounded_rectangle([20, 20, 780, 760], radius=32, fill='#114b29', outline='#061a0e', width=6)\nimg.save('test_size.png')\nprint('Base works!')\n\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Test basic 800x780 canvas setup"}}]}
