{"step_index":149,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T08:36:51Z","input_tokens":3245,"cache_read_tokens":157315,"output_tokens":1229,"thinking":"The task is to build an interactive HTML version of the card sort game, incorporating the new 8x20 map. The design must replicate the existing game mechanics: single-tap column interaction for card retrieval based on color matching, prioritizing matching columns and then empty columns.\n\n\nInitial focus is on clarifying card clearing mechanics in the 8x20 grid, specifically defining color-based column clearing conditions. Pure columns, where all cards share the same color, clearing when reaching a configurable threshold like 6 or 8 cards, or when all remaining cards of that color are gathered. This clearing mechanic will be similar to existing game modes with full stack bursts. Dynamic vertical offsets for card positioning based on column length will be implemented in the Javascript.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"node -e \"\nconst grid = [\n    'BBBBBBBB',\n    'BBRRRRBB',\n    'BRRRRRRB',\n    'RRWWWWRR',\n    'RRWWWWRR',\n    'RWWWRRWR',\n    'RWWWRRWR',\n    'RRRRRRRR',\n    'RRRRRRRR',\n    'BRRRRRRB',\n    'BSSSSSSB',\n    'BSDSSDSS',\n    'BSDSSDSS',\n    'BSSSSSSB',\n    'BSSSSSSB',\n    'BGGGGGGB',\n    'GGGGGGGG',\n    'GGGGGGGG',\n    'BYYYYYYB',\n    'YYYYYYYY'\n];\nconst counts = {};\nfor (const r of grid) {\n  for (const c of r) {\n    counts[c] = (counts[c] || 0) + 1;\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('Total cards:', grid.length * 8, counts);\n\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Count cards of each color in Mushroom map"}}]}
